; llama-token-handle.fk — a llama3.2:3b token with the DECODE LOOP IN A FORM CELL.
;
; WHAT MOVED, AND WHAT DID NOT. metal_first_token.sh generates real tokens from this blob and has
; since 2026-07-21. It does it by writing out a 1000-line Swift program at run time: that program
; holds the pool, the layer loop, the KV cache, the barriers, the command buffer and the readback.
; Every kernel it runs is the body's, and the harness says so honestly — but the RECIPE, the order
; in which 452 dispatches happen and what each one is bound to, lived in Swift. This cell is that
; recipe, in the body. There is no swiftc, no .metallib on disk, no runner binary. The only host
; crossing is metal_buf_from_file reading the model file's bytes.
;
; NOT ONE KERNEL IS NEW EXCEPT ONE, AND THAT ONE DOES NO ARITHMETIC. The unit is
; q6m-msl-unit + q4m-msl-unit + ldm-msl-unit, exactly as first-token.fk's ft-emit-msl assembles it
; (minus the speed appendices, which are twins of the attestants and not needed to be right). The
; single addition is form_copy_off_f32, and the reason it exists is a property of the door rather
; than of llama:
;
;   THE DOOR BINDS A HANDLE AT THAT HANDLE'S OWN OFFSET. metal_enqueue's binding string carries
;   handles, and the carrier binds each at fk_buf_meta[h].view_off — a FIXED offset decided when
;   the handle was made. The Swift bound the KV cache at (layer * maxpos + pos) * kvd * 4, an
;   offset that changes every token. There is no primitive that makes a view of a device buffer at
;   a new offset, so a cache write cannot be expressed as a bind. It can be expressed as a MOVE:
;   the matvec writes k and v to a scratch at offset 0, RoPE rotates them there, and a copy kernel
;   places them in the cache at doff = pos * kvd. A copy performs no arithmetic — no add, no
;   multiply, no rounding — so the attestant's numbers are untouched and the twin question does not
;   arise. It is authored HERE rather than in llama-decode-msl.fk on purpose: that cell's text is
;   the cache key metal_first_token.sh compiles against, and a kernel appended there would
;   invalidate the proven lane's pipeline cache for a reason that has nothing to do with it.
;
; THE BIT-EXACT SET, AND WHY THE LINE SITS EXACTLY THERE. First cut (2026-08-04 morning): the
; attestants only, one thread apiece, serial encoder — 0.855 tok/s, and the header here said the
; cooperative twins were unreachable because metal_enqueue offered dispatchThreads alone.
; The door's second growth removed that: dispatch_mode 1 makes the op's threads argument the GROUP
; COUNT with threads_per_group exact (refused past the pipeline ceiling, never clamped), and
; metal_batch_concurrent opens a concurrent batch whose hazards THIS CELL declares per dispatch
; via barrier_before. So this cell now dispatches the twins whose cells claim EQUALITY, not an
; epsilon: form_rmsnorm_tg_f32 (same fold order, staged operands, BIT FOR BIT, n <= 4096, one
; threadgroup — both honored by mode 1), form_rope_pair_f32 (a thread map, not an order; hd even),
; form_argmax_part/comb_f32 (comparison and selection only, ties still to the lowest index). The
; epsilon-bearing matvec twins (split/lane/slot) are NOT taken: a rate bought with an epsilon
; belongs to a rung that states its bound, and the matvecs here stay the serial attestants. The
; barrier plan is the proven Swift lane's, translated to barrier_before (see the dispatch section);
; none of this changes one expression, which is why the recorded 12-id stream is REQUIRED to
; survive this rung unchanged and the band checks that it does.
;
; EVERY NUMBER IS THE FILE'S. block_count, embedding_length, feed_forward_length, head counts,
; rope dimension_count, rope.freq_base and layer_norm_rms_epsilon come from the metadata KVs
; (gmt-u32 / gmt-f32); every tensor's offset, both dimensions and its ggml type come from the
; tensor table (egg-*); every tensor's byte length is priced by wtr-bytes from that tensor's own
; declared type. Nothing is typed in. The two float constants Metal wants as raw bytes — eps and
; freq_base — go through metal-door.fk's md-f32-bits, and the third, the attention scale, is
; 1/sqrt(head_dim) folded from head_dim the file declares.
;
; TIED EMBEDDINGS ARE READ, NOT ASSUMED. If the table has no output.weight the unembedding IS
; token_embd, and that is what lth-out-tv returns. A file that has one uses it.
;
; ONE SYNC PER TOKEN, and the loop never waits. metal_enqueue returns without committing, so the
; whole token — embed gather, 28 layers, final norm, the vocabulary projection and the greedy pick
; — accumulates in one command buffer, and metal_buf_read of FOUR BYTES is the single drain. That
; shape is what the seam measurement bought: at ~2 us per crossing a Form cell can afford 452 of
; them per token, and at ~112 us per blocking dispatch it could not afford eight.
;
; Kin: form-stdlib/metal-door.fk (md-bind, md-f32-bits — the bytes the door reads),
;      native/metal/whole-tensor-residency.fk (wtr-bytes — the byte pricing per ggml type),
;      form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk (gmt-* — the metadata reach), form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk (egg-*),
;      form-stdlib/q6k-msl.fk / q4k-msl.fk / llama-decode-msl.fk (every kernel but the copy),
;      native/metal/metal_first_token.sh (the attestant this cell must agree with).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/q6k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/q4k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk form-stdlib/q6k-msl.fk form-stdlib/q4k-msl.fk form-stdlib/transformer-numerics.fk form-stdlib/transformer-block.fk form-stdlib/llama-numerics.fk form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk form-stdlib/trig.fk form-stdlib/tensor-ir.fk form-stdlib/jit-tensor-emit.fk form-stdlib/llama-decode-msl.fk form-stdlib/qk-matvec-split.fk form-stdlib/qk-matvec-lane.fk form-stdlib/qk-matvec-slot.fk form-stdlib/qk-matmul-batch.fk native/metal/whole-tensor-residency.fk form-stdlib/gguf-tensor-index.fk form-stdlib/metal-door.fk form-stdlib/native-model-tensor-ledger.bml
;
; Proven by: form/native/metal/tests/llama-token-handle-band.fk

(do
    ; ================= the translation unit =================
    ; The pure move the door's fixed-offset binding makes necessary. No arithmetic, so nothing to
    ; attest against: dst[doff + i] = src[i] is the identity with a shifted destination.
    (defn lth-copy-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* s [[buffer(0)]], device float* d [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& doff [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; d[doff + i] = s[i]; }")))

    ; qml-msl-header leads the file for the same reason ft-emit-msl gives: a #include is only legal
    ; at the top, and it is emitted WITHOUT `using namespace metal;` so ldm-msl-round's `round`
    ; still resolves to the body's and not the library's.
    (defn lth-msl ()
        (str_concat (qml-msl-header)
        (str_concat (q6m-msl-unit "form_q6k_dequant_f32" "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (q4m-msl-unit "form_q4k_dequant_f32" "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (ldm-msl-unit)
                    (lth-copy-msl "form_copy_off_f32"))))))
    ; ldm-msl-unit already carries the four bit-exact twins (ldm-msl-fast): form_rmsnorm_tg_f32,
    ; form_rope_pair_f32, form_argmax_part_f32, form_argmax_comb_f32. Nothing new is emitted for
    ; the fast path — the door grew the shape they need, not the kernels.

    ; ================= the file's own numbers =================
    (defn lth-src (path) (eqr-of-file path 0 (wtr-header-window)))

    ; A tensor VIEW: (handle, rows, cols, ggml-type, exact mapped bytes). rows is dim1 and cols is dim0, because GGUF's
    ; dim0 is the fastest-varying axis — the matrix is dim1 rows of dim0 columns.
    (defn lth-tv (src base path name)
        (do (let off (egg-find-tensor src name))
            (list (metal_buf_from_file path
                      (add base (egg-ti-dataoff src off))
                      (wtr-bytes src off))
                  (wtr-dim1 src off)
                  (egg-ti-dim0 src off)
                  (egg-ti-type src off)
                  (wtr-bytes src off))))

    (defn lth-tv-h  (t) (nth t 0))
    (defn lth-tv-r  (t) (nth t 1))
    (defn lth-tv-c  (t) (nth t 2))
    (defn lth-tv-ty (t) (nth t 3))
    (defn lth-tv-bytes (t) (nth t 4))

    (defn lth-blk (l suffix) (str_concat "blk." (str_concat (int_to_str l) (str_concat "." suffix))))

    ; A tensor view from a KNOWN record offset — the collected-walk twin of lth-tv. Same four
    ; fields, no walk.
    (defn lth-tv-at (src base path off)
        (list (metal_buf_from_file path
                  (add base (egg-ti-dataoff src off))
                  (wtr-bytes src off))
              (wtr-dim1 src off)
              (egg-ti-dim0 src off)
              (egg-ti-type src off)
              (wtr-bytes src off)))

    ; The nine tensors one llama block reaches: the two norms and the seven projections.
    ;
    ; THE LOOKUPS ARE COLLECTED, NOT SEARCHED (2026-08-04). The first cut called egg-find-tensor
    ; 252 times — each a full parse of the 255-record table — and that was ~73 s of a 96 s band:
    ; the O(n^2) gguf-tensor-index.fk names, arrived at again. Nine gti-offs-with walks now carry
    ; every block's record offset away at once, and a per-layer lookup is a 28-entry list scan.
    ; egg-find-tensor stays for the four model-level singles, where it is exactly right.
    (defn lth-suffixes ()
        (list ".attn_norm.weight" ".attn_q.weight" ".attn_k.weight" ".attn_v.weight"
              ".attn_output.weight" ".ffn_norm.weight" ".ffn_gate.weight" ".ffn_up.weight"
              ".ffn_down.weight"))
    (defn lth-tabs-go (src sfx acc)
        (if (eq (len sfx) 0) (reverse acc)
            (lth-tabs-go src (tail sfx) (cons (gti-offs-with src (head sfx)) acc))))
    (defn lth-tabs (src) (lth-tabs-go src (lth-suffixes) (empty)))

    (defn lth-layer-go (src base path l tabs acc)
        (if (eq (len tabs) 0) (reverse acc)
            (lth-layer-go src base path l (tail tabs)
                (cons (lth-tv-at src base path (gti-off-for (head tabs) l)) acc))))
    (defn lth-layer (src base path l tabs) (lth-layer-go src base path l tabs (empty)))

    (defn lth-layers-go (src base path l n tabs acc)
        (if (ge l n) acc
            (lth-layers-go src base path (add l 1) n tabs
                (append acc (list (lth-layer src base path l tabs))))))
    (defn lth-layers (src base path l n acc)
        (lth-layers-go src base path l n (lth-tabs src) acc))

    ; TIED IS A FACT ABOUT THE TABLE. No output.weight in the file means the unembedding IS
    ; token_embd; egg-find-tensor answers -1 and that -1 is what decides, not a convention.
    (defn lth-out-tv (src base path)
        (if (eq (egg-find-tensor src "output.weight") (sub 0 1))
            (lth-tv src base path "token_embd.weight")
            (lth-tv src base path "output.weight")))

    ; ================= the pool =================
    ; pipes: 0 q6dq 1 q4dq 2 q6mv 3 q4mv 4 rms 5 rope 6 attn 7 swiglu 8 add 9 argmax 10 copy
    (defn lth-pipes (msl)
        (list (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_decode_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_swiglu_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_add_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_copy_off_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_tg_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_pair_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_part_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_comb_f32")))

    (defn lth-pipe-ok? (ps) (if (eq (len ps) 0) true (if (eq (head ps) 0) false (lth-pipe-ok? (tail ps)))))

    ; bufs: 0 X 1 Xb 2 Q 3 Ks 4 Vs 5 Attn 6 Proj 7 Ffn 8 Gate 9 Up 10 Act 11 Logits 12 Scratch
    ;       13 OutI 14 OutV
    ; ALLOCATED ONCE, before any token, and never reallocated — the pool the seam measurement said
    ; a decode loop must have. bScratch is 2*nHead*maxpos: the attention kernel keeps scores at
    ; h*sstride and their exponentials at (nq+h)*sstride, with sstride = maxpos.
    (defn lth-alloc-sizes (sizes)
        (if (eq (len sizes) 0) (list)
            (cons (metal_buf_alloc (head sizes))
                  (lth-alloc-sizes (tail sizes)))))
    (defn lth-bufs (dModel dFF vocabN nHead maxpos)
        (lth-alloc-sizes
            (nmtl-llama-scratch-sizes dModel dFF vocabN nHead maxpos)))

    ; One K and one V buffer PER LAYER. Per-layer rather than one big cache because the door binds
    ; at a handle's own offset: the layer stride can be a handle, the position stride cannot.
    (defn lth-cache (n kvd maxpos acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc (lth-cache (sub n 1) kvd maxpos (append acc (list (metal_buf_alloc (nmtl-llama-cache-bytes kvd maxpos)))))))

    (defn lth-list-handles (tvs)
        (if (eq (len tvs) 0) (list)
            (cons (lth-tv-h (head tvs)) (lth-list-handles (tail tvs)))))
    (defn lth-list-sizes (tvs)
        (if (eq (len tvs) 0) (list)
            (cons (lth-tv-bytes (head tvs)) (lth-list-sizes (tail tvs)))))
    (defn lth-layer-handles (layers)
        (if (eq (len layers) 0) (list)
            (append (lth-list-handles (head layers))
                    (lth-layer-handles (tail layers)))))
    (defn lth-layer-sizes (layers)
        (if (eq (len layers) 0) (list)
            (append (lth-list-sizes (head layers))
                    (lth-layer-sizes (tail layers)))))

    ; ================= the dispatches =================
    ; EVERY MODE-0 DISPATCH CAPS ITS GROUP AT 256 — the proven lane's own FORM_METAL_TG default,
    ; measured there, not re-derived here. With tpg 0 this door fills groups to the pipeline's
    ; 1024 ceiling, and on the memory-bound serial-fold matvecs that costs real occupancy:
    ; witnessed on this cell 2026-08-04, 1083 ms/token at the ceiling against 388 ms/token in the
    ; oracle's recorded attestant run at 256.
    ; EVERY BINDING CARRIES THE base+16 TAIL and every batch is CONCURRENT (door's second growth,
    ; 2026-08-04). Hazards are DECLARED BY THIS CELL via barrier_before — the door guesses nothing.
    ; The barrier plan is the proven Swift lane's, translated: that lane put a barrier AFTER each
    ; dispatch except where the next one was independent (q/k/v read the same normed vector and
    ; write disjoint buffers; so do gate/up and the two RoPEs), so barrier_before here is exactly
    ; "was there a barrier between my predecessor and me" — and nothing about the arithmetic
    ; changes, which is why the recorded 12-id stream is required to survive this rung unchanged.
    ;
    ; THE TWINS DISPATCHED HERE ARE THE BIT-EXACT ONES ONLY: the cooperative RMSNorm (same fold
    ; order, staged operands — BIT FOR BIT its attestant, radius n <= 4096, one threadgroup, both
    ; honored via dispatch_mode 1), RoPE at pair grain (a thread map, not an order; hd must be
    ; even), and the two-stage argmax (comparison and selection only, ties still to the lowest
    ; index). The epsilon-bearing matvec twins (split/lane/slot) are NOT taken — a rate bought
    ; with an epsilon belongs to a rung with its own stated bound.
    (defn lth-mv (ps tv xh yh bb)
        (metal_enqueue (if (eq (lth-tv-ty tv) 14) (nth ps 2) (nth ps 3))
                       (md-bind16 (list (lth-tv-h tv) xh yh) (list (lth-tv-r tv) (lth-tv-c tv))
                                  256 0 0 bb)
                       (lth-tv-r tv)))

    (defn lth-dq (ps tv yh off n bb)
        (metal_enqueue (if (eq (lth-tv-ty tv) 14) (nth ps 0) (nth ps 1))
                       (md-bind16 (list (lth-tv-h tv) yh) (list off n) 256 0 0 bb)
                       n))

    ; ONE threadgroup of 256, exactly, and the kernel's whole radius honored by the mode that
    ; cannot split it: threads argument = group count = 1.
    (defn lth-rms (ps xh gtv yh n epsBits bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 11)
                       (md-bind16 (list xh (lth-tv-h gtv) yh) (list n epsBits) 256 0 1 bb)
                       1))

    (defn lth-rope (ps vh ropeH nh hd pos baseBits bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 12)
                       (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH) (list nh hd pos baseBits) 256 0 0 bb)
                       (mul nh (div hd 2))))

    (defn lth-attn (ps qh kh vh yh sh npos nq nkv hd scaleBits sstride bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 6)
                       (md-bind16 (list qh kh vh yh sh) (list npos nq nkv hd scaleBits sstride)
                                  256 0 0 bb)
                       nq))

    (defn lth-elem (ps p ah bh yh n bb)
        (metal_enqueue p (md-bind16 (list ah bh yh) (list n) 256 0 0 bb) n))

    (defn lth-copy (ps sh dh n doff bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 10) (md-bind16 (list sh dh) (list n doff) 256 0 0 bb) n))

    ; greedy selection in two stages: 1024 contiguous chunks, then one group folds the partials
    ; ascending — the tie rule survives the split by construction (llama-decode-msl.fk).
    (defn lth-argmax (ps bs vocabN)
        (do (metal_enqueue (nth ps 13)
                           (md-bind16 (list (nth bs 11) (nth bs 15) (nth bs 16))
                                      (list vocabN 1024) 256 0 0 1)
                           1024)
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 14)
                           (md-bind16 (list (nth bs 15) (nth bs 16) (nth bs 13) (nth bs 14))
                                      (list 1024) 1024 0 1 1)
                           1)))

    ; ================= one block =================
    ; The order is jte-llama-blk's, op for op, and it is the order the Swift attestant walks. The
    ; door's encoder is SERIAL, so each dispatch's writes are visible to the next and an activation
    ; never leaves the device between two of them.
    (defn lth-block (ps bs geo lay ck cv pos)
        (do
            (lth-rms ps (nth bs 0) (nth lay 0) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 1) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 2) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 2) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 3) 0)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 3) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 4) 0)
            (lth-rope ps (nth bs 2) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 4) pos (nth geo 9) 1)
            (lth-rope ps (nth bs 3) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) pos (nth geo 9) 0)
            (lth-copy ps (nth bs 3) ck (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 1)
            (lth-copy ps (nth bs 4) cv (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 0)
            (lth-attn ps (nth bs 2) ck cv (nth bs 5) (nth bs 12)
                      (add pos 1) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 10) (nth geo 6) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 4) (nth bs 5) (nth bs 6) 1)
            (lth-elem ps (nth ps 8) (nth bs 0) (nth bs 6) (nth bs 0) (nth geo 0) 1)
            (lth-rms ps (nth bs 0) (nth lay 5) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 6) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 8) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 7) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 9) 0)
            (lth-elem ps (nth ps 7) (nth bs 8) (nth bs 9) (nth bs 10) (nth geo 1) 1)
            (lth-mv ps (nth lay 8) (nth bs 10) (nth bs 7) 1)
            (lth-elem ps (nth ps 8) (nth bs 0) (nth bs 7) (nth bs 0) (nth geo 0) 1)
            1))

    (defn lth-blocks (ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos l n)
        (if (ge l n) 1
            (do (lth-block ps bs geo (nth lays l) (nth cks l) (nth cvs l) pos)
                (lth-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos (add l 1) n))))

    ; ================= one token =================
    ; geo: 0 dModel 1 dFF 2 nHead 3 nKV 4 headDim 5 kvd 6 maxpos 7 vocabN 8 epsBits 9 baseBits
    ;      10 scaleBits 11 ropeH 12 nLayer
    (defn lth-attn-scale-bits (headDim)
        (md-f32-bits (div 1.0 (math_sqrt (add headDim 0.0)))))
    ;
    ; The final norm's GAIN is output_norm.weight, not the unembedding — kept separate so the tied
    ; case cannot quietly feed the projection's own bytes to the normalizer.
    (defn lth-head (ps bs geo onormTv projTv)
        (do
            (lth-rms ps (nth bs 0) onormTv (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (lth-mv ps projTv (nth bs 1) (nth bs 11) 1)
            (lth-argmax ps bs (nth geo 7))
            0))

    (defn lth-u32 (s)
        (add (str_byte_at s 0)
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s 1) 256)
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s 2) 65536)
             (mul (str_byte_at s 3) 16777216)))))

    ; ONE forward pass: embed, every block, the head, then FOUR BYTES back. metal_buf_read is the
    ; only drain in the whole token — it syncs first by construction, so the id it returns cannot be
    ; a stale buffer read before the work that fills it.
    (defn lth-forward (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos)
        (do
            (metal_batch_concurrent)
            (lth-dq ps embTv (nth bs 0) (mul id (nth geo 0)) (nth geo 0) 0)
            (lth-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos 0 (nth geo 12))
            (lth-head ps bs geo onormTv projTv)
            (lth-u32 (metal_buf_read (nth bs 13) 0 4))))

    ; ================= the loop, in the body =================
    ; Greedy: the id that comes back is the id that goes in, at the next position. The KV cache is
    ; where the history lives, and it lives on the device across every step.
    (defn lth-generate (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos n acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (do (let nid (lth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos))
                (lth-generate ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv
                              nid (add pos 1) (sub n 1) (append acc (list nid))))))

    ; Feeding a PROMPT: the same forward at each position, but the answer is discarded until the
    ; last one — that last id is the model's first real prediction.
    (defn lth-prefill (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv ids pos)
        (if (eq (len ids) 1)
            (list (lth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos) pos)
            (do (lth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos)
                (lth-prefill ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (tail ids) (add pos 1)))))
    0)
